  "notes": "114:20-23 not glossed (Al-Muyassar's «أوحينا» is first person). 115:9-11 uses As-Sa'di for «العليم» (Al-Muyassar's text reads «الحليم» here). A book for «الكتاب مفصلا», geometric for «كلمت ربك», two paths for «يضلوك» (leaving before the Name), light for «بالمهتدين». No motif on the Prophet ﷺ. STAGING v4: c1 (114-115) kept ambient (the Book, the words of your Lord, His names); a pan added on 114:19 (motion check). c2 (116-117): most of the people on earth as an uncountable crowd in dark robes (no women drawn in a blamed group) that walks on (following conjecture and their forefathers, Al-Muyassar) and speaks on 116:18; the few guided as 2 believers. The condition addressed to the Prophet (116:1-10) is not acted, he is not shown. Crowd plate for 116:3 (ends before the Name); the light plate is moved from 117:9 (His pronoun) to 117:11 (the guided)."
